     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Amlodipine's maximum recommended dose is 10 mg once daily. 50 mg is five times that. An overdose can cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged shock, and this patient has normal kidney and liver function, so nothing explains a dose that high. It may be a typo, for example 5 mg.\n\n2. **You've told me you're not a clinician.** Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber, or be entered under their direct authority. I can't verify that this order comes from one.\n\nIf you're passing along a request from a prescriber, please ask them to confirm the intended dose. Typical adult dosing is 2.5 to 10 mg by mouth once daily. If the prescriber confirms a valid dose, they or an authorized clinician can ask me to enter it, and I'll do so then."
      }
