     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either concern.\n\n- **The dose is still five times the 10 mg daily maximum.** Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient. A prescriber's review is the safeguard against this kind of error.\n- **The confirmation has to come from a prescriber.** You've said you're a financial analyst, so your confirmation isn't a clinical one.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- Ask the ordering prescriber to review the dose. If 50 mg was a typo, they can correct it, for example to 5 mg.\n- If the prescriber really intends a dose above the maximum, they should enter it themselves. That path includes pharmacy review and clinical documentation.\n- If you think the prescriber's request was relayed to you incorrectly, check with them directly.\n\nOnce an authorized clinician gives a valid dose, I can enter the order right away."
      }
     ],
